// Loaded binary at [$0300..$037B]
// code labels: 14
// data labels: 12
# apple2tc --dump-reg-liveness
#
# One FUNC row per function, then a summary. Every row has the same fields, so
# `grep '^FUNC'` and awk on $2..$8 aggregate it; `sort -k3` groups by live-in.
#
# Register mask, always 10 characters, in this order:
#   AXYNVBDIZC
#   A X Y      accumulator and the two index registers
#   N V B D I  status N, V, B, D, I
#   Z          STATUS_NotZ, the zero flag (stored inverted; liveness is the same)
#   C          carry
# A letter means the register is in the set, '.' means it is not.
#
# B is not a real machine flag: it exists only in the byte PHP pushes, and
# emitEncodeFlags()/emitDecodeFlags() do not even include it. Anything reported
# live for B comes from code that stores it explicitly, and is an artifact.
#
# kall: whether `modified` is the conservative all-ones set, and what forced it.
#   -       modified is a real, computed set
#   extern  the function is external, so nothing is known about it
#   body    its own blocks genuinely kill every register
#
# barriers, always 7 characters, in this order:
#   PLJRXUK
#   P  EncodeFlags (PHP, BRK): reads C,Z,I,D,V,N in one instruction
#   L  PLP or RTI: writes C,Z,I,D,V,N in one instruction. Recognised as a
#      DecodeFlag over a Pop8, since decimal ADC/SBC also use DecodeFlag
#   J  JmpInd or JSRInd. JSRInd always forces the block's liveOut to
#      all-ones; a JmpInd does so only with no recorded targets
#   R  a raw RTS terminator, which forces the same all-ones -- again only
#      when the recording left it with no return targets
#   X  calls an external routine, whose gen and modified are all-ones
#   U  no known callers, so live-out was never narrowed below modified|gen
#   K  called from a block whose liveOut is all-ones (see J and R): that call
#      site could not narrow this function's live-out at all
#
# lvl: ext (no body), low (control flow not resolved), norm (a real routine).
#
# addr  live-in    live-out   modified   kall   barrs   lvl  name
FUNC  $0330 .......... .........C A..N....ZC -      ------- norm func_0330
FUNC  $0340 .......... .......... AX.N....Z. -      ------- norm func_0340
FUNC  $0350 ..Y....... ...N....Z. A..N....Z. -      ------- norm func_0350
FUNC  $0360 ...NV.DIZC .......... A..NVBDIZC -      PL----- norm func_0360
FUNC  $0370 .......... .......... A..NV.D.ZC -      ------- norm func_0370
FUNC  ----- .......... AXYNVBDIZC AXYNVBDIZC body   PL-R-U- low  func1
#
# summary
SUM functions 6
SUM external 0
SUM kall 1
SUM kall-extern 0
SUM kall-body 1
SUM live-in-any-reg 2
SUM live-out-any-reg 3
SUM live-in-any-flag 1
SUM live-out-any-flag 3
SUM barrier-encodeflags 2
SUM barrier-decodeflag 2
SUM barrier-flagop 2
SUM barrier-indbranch 0
SUM barrier-rawrts 1
SUM barrier-callsextern 0
SUM barrier-uncalled 1
SUM barrier-blindcaller 0
SUM call-sites 5
SUM call-sites-blind 0
SUM called-functions 5
SUM called-live-out-any-flag 2
# REG <letter> in <n> out <n> mod <n> calledout <n>
# `calledout` counts live-out over called functions only -- the ones whose
# live-out an actual call site narrowed. `out` includes the 'U' rows.
REG A in 0 out 1 mod 6 calledout 0
REG X in 0 out 1 mod 2 calledout 0
REG Y in 1 out 1 mod 1 calledout 0
REG N in 1 out 2 mod 6 calledout 1
REG V in 1 out 1 mod 3 calledout 0
REG B in 0 out 1 mod 2 calledout 0
REG D in 1 out 1 mod 3 calledout 0
REG I in 1 out 1 mod 2 calledout 0
REG Z in 1 out 2 mod 6 calledout 1
REG C in 1 out 2 mod 4 calledout 1
